  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mugeshsingh vs The State Of Tamil Nadu on 4 November, 2024 Author: M.Nirmal Kumar Bench: M.Nirmal Kumar Crl.O.P.(MD) Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 04.11.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice M.Nirmal Kumar Crl.O.P.(MD)No.18916 of 2024 and Crl.M.P.(MD) No.11696 of 2024 1.Mugeshsingh 2.Anandh Singh ... -vs- 1.The State of Tamil Nadu, Rep. by the Inspector of Police, Sessions Court Police Station, Trichy City. (Crime No.238 of 2024) 2.Syed Ibrahim ... R Petition filed under Section 528 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Sur 2023, seeking to call for the records relating to the F.I.R. in Crime N 2024, dated 28.06.2024, on the file of the first respondent Police, and same as against the petitioners / A1 and A2 are concerned. ____________ Page 1 of 5 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O. Mugeshsingh vs The State Of Tamil Nadu on 4 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/84207757/ 1 For Petitioners : Mr.S.Balasubramanian For R1 : Mr.A.Thiruvadi Kumar Additional Public Prosecu Order",
    "facts": "The petitioners filed the Criminal Original Petition seeking to quash the F.I.R. in Crime No.238 of 2024, registered against them for the offences under Sections 273 and 328 I.P.C. and Sections 6(a) and 24(1) of the Cigarette and other Tobacco Products Act, 2003, on the file of the first respondent Police. 2. The case against the petitioners is that on 28.06.2024, at 12.30 p.m., the Food Safety Officer conducted an inspection in a Paan Shop belonging to the petitioners. Hence, the petitioners prayed for quashing of the F.I.R. 4.",
    "arguments": ". The contention of the petitioners is that, in this case, the mandatory procedures contemplated under Sections 42(2), 42(3) and 47 of the Food Safety and Standards Act have not been followed and the report should have been sent within 14 days from the date of receipt of the samples to the Commissioner of Food Safety for sanctioning prosecution, but the same has not been followed in this case."
  },
